IMPORT prelude

-- Platform Workers Act 2024 (Singapore) -- who is covered: platform service (s 3 and the First Schedule), platform operator
-- (s 4), platform worker (s 5), management control (s 6 and the Second Schedule); no contracting out of association rights
-- (s 7); priority of platform workers' earnings in insolvency (ss 16 to 18); and the ballot needed before a strike (s 36).
--
-- Edition: the Act as enacted (Act 30 of 2024), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/PWA2024.txt. Not a revised
-- edition.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 21 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository, 10 to 14 times each for ss 3, 4 and 5:
-- other Acts (CPF, Work Injury Compensation, Income Tax) extend to "platform workers" by reference to these definitions.
-- SCOPED to coverage, which is what those Acts borrow. Not encoded: notification and records duties (Part 2 Divisions 1 and
-- 2 beyond mention), platform work associations' registration and governance (Part 3 beyond ss 7 and 36), administrative
-- penalties, enforcement, and the amendments to other Acts.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Platform Workers Act 2024 -- coverage`

§§ `3 and the First Schedule -- platform service`

-- s 3(1): a "platform service" is a service SPECIFIED IN THE FIRST SCHEDULE, provided in Singapore via a platform by an
-- operator exercising management control. First Schedule para 1: "(a) delivery service; (b) ride-hail service." Ride-hail
-- excludes taxi call-booking, permitted car-pooling, and licensed cross-border Singapore-Malaysia services.
--
-- Only two services are covered. A cleaner, tutor, handyman or freelancer on an app platform is outside the Act however
-- tightly the app controls them, until the Schedule is amended.
DECLARE ServiceType IS ONE OF
    `food or parcel delivery`
    `private-hire ride-hail`
    `taxi call-booking`
    `home cleaning`
    `tutoring`
    `cross-border ride-hail by a licensed provider`

GIVEN `the service` IS A ServiceType
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the service is a scheduled platform service` IF
    CONSIDER `the service`
    WHEN `food or parcel delivery` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `private-hire ride-hail` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `6 and the Second Schedule -- management control`

-- s 6(1): A exercises management control over B if ALL of: (a) A uses data about service users and about the individuals
-- performing tasks, for a specified purpose -- deciding B's eligibility, allocating tasks, or fixing B's pay; (b) that use
-- "does not involve human intervention on a regular or routine basis"; and (c) A imposes on B any requirement, prohibition or
-- restriction in the Second Schedule: rules on when, how or to what standard to serve; a bar on negotiating price with users;
-- a bar on building one's own clientele; a restriction on choosing hours or number of tasks; or SYSTEMATIC incentives or
-- penalties to keep B working or working more.
-- (3): requirements imposed under written law do not count for (c).
-- (4): management control is PRESUMED, unless disproved, where B works under a platform work agreement and must access tasks
-- through A's app or website.
DECLARE Control HAS
    `uses data algorithmically to decide eligibility, allocation or pay` IS A BOOLEAN
    `routine human intervention in that use` IS A BOOLEAN
    `imposes a Second Schedule requirement other than one required by law` IS A BOOLEAN
    `tasks are accessed through the operator's app or website under a platform work agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the operator disproves control` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the control` IS A Control
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the operator exercises management control` IF
        (    `the control`'s `uses data algorithmically to decide eligibility, allocation or pay`
         AND NOT `the control`'s `routine human intervention in that use`
         AND `the control`'s `imposes a Second Schedule requirement other than one required by law`)
    OR  (    `the control`'s `tasks are accessed through the operator's app or website under a platform work agreement`
         AND NOT `the control`'s `the operator disproves control`)

DECLARE Restriction IS ONE OF
    `service quality standards`
    `no negotiating fares with customers`
    `no building one's own clientele`
    `limits on hours or number of tasks`
    `systematic incentives to keep working`
    `a road traffic rule the law requires`
    `a one-off thank-you bonus`

GIVEN `the restriction` IS A Restriction
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the restriction is in the Second Schedule` IF
    CONSIDER `the restriction`
    WHEN `a road traffic rule the law requires` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a one-off thank-you bonus` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `4, 5 -- operator and worker`

-- s 5(1): a "platform worker" is an individual who (a) has an agreement, "whether written or oral and whether express or
-- implied", with a platform operator to provide a platform service; (b) is subject to its management control; (c) derives
-- payment or benefit in kind; and (d) "is in Singapore when providing the platform service". (2): "agreement" does not
-- include a contract of service -- EMPLOYEES are not platform workers.
-- s 4(2): an operator does not stop being one by subcontracting the service or the management control.
DECLARE Worker HAS
    `the service` IS A ServiceType
    `has an agreement with the operator` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is an employee under a contract of service` IS A BOOLEAN
    `subject to management control` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is paid or receives benefits in kind` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in Singapore when working` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the worker` IS A Worker
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is a platform worker` IF
        `the service is a scheduled platform service` (`the worker`'s `the service`)
    AND `the worker`'s `has an agreement with the operator`
    AND NOT `the worker`'s `is an employee under a contract of service`
    AND `the worker`'s `subject to management control`
    AND `the worker`'s `is paid or receives benefits in kind`
    AND `the worker`'s `in Singapore when working`

GIVEN `subcontracted the service or the control` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the operator ceases to be a platform operator` IF
    FALSE

§§ `7 -- no contracting out`

-- s 7(1): every term of an agreement "which purports to restrict or exclude, in any way, the right" to join or take part in a
-- registered platform work association, or to organise one, "is void".
GIVEN `the term restricts association rights` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the term is void` IF
    `the term restricts association rights`

§§ `16 to 18 -- earnings in the operator's insolvency`

-- s 18(2) (and ss 16, 17 alike): the following rank after the IRDA preferential debts up to s 352(1)(g) and before (h):
-- (a) FIRST, earnings payable to platform workers (capped by order, (3)); (b) SECOND, work injury compensation; (c) THIRD,
-- platform-worker CPF contributions for a 12-month window around the order.
DECLARE PWClaim IS ONE OF
    `unpaid platform earnings`
    `work injury compensation`
    `platform CPF contributions`

GIVEN `the claim` IS A PWClaim
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the rank among platform claims` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the claim`
    WHEN `unpaid platform earnings` THEN 1
    WHEN `work injury compensation` THEN 2
    WHEN `platform CPF contributions` THEN 3

§§ `36 -- strikes`

-- s 36(1): a registered platform work association must not start, promote, organise or finance a strike "without obtaining the
-- consent, by secret ballot, of the majority of the members so affected" -- association and executive $3,000. (3): MEMBERS who
-- take part in a strike without that ballot, or contrary to the rules -- $2,000 each.
GIVEN `members affected` IS A NUMBER, `votes in favour by secret ballot` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the strike is lawfully authorised` IF
    (`votes in favour by secret ballot` TIMES 2) GREATER THAN `members affected`

GIVEN `authorised by ballot` IS A BOOLEAN, `took part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the member commits the section 36 offence` IF
    `took part` AND NOT `authorised by ballot`
